Ok, here's the scoop on those messages you get when you do
regular sacrifices to your own god.  (I'm not dealing with
unicorns, conversions, etc.)  This is from the code itself.

SPOILER ALERT

You can be in one of three states with your god:  the god is angry; 
you're timing out between prayers; and you're in good stead, getting
brownie points.

If your god is angry, and you get the message...

"You have a feeling of inadequacy."
  Your sacrifice was too small, and your god's anger has not changed.

"The gods seem slightly mollified."
  Your god is still angry, but less so.  
  If you have negative luck, it will increase by one.

"The gods seem mollified."
  Your god is no longer angry with you.
  If you have negative luck, it will increase to zero.


If you are timing out between prayers, and you get the message...

No message beside the sacrifice being consumed.
  Your sacrifice was too small, and your prayer count has not changed.

"You have a hopeful feeling."
  Your prayer count has decreased, but not zeroed out.
  If you have negative luck, it will increase by one.

"You have a feeling of reconciliation."
  Your pray count has reached zero.  You can safely pray again.
  If you have negative luck, it will increase to zero.


If you're working on your god's good side, and you get the message...

"You glimpse a four-leaf clover at your feet."
  Your luck has increased.

"An object appears at your feet."
  YES!!!  An artifact!


You may ask, how much is a corpse worth to your god?  I can't tell;
it's a complex formula base on a lot of monster attributes.  Suffice
it to say, if you thing the monster is tough, it's probably worth more.



